+**Keep on top.** The pin button in every title bar (control id `core/always-on-top`) toggles `alwaysOnTop`; `windowManager.setAlwaysOnTop( id, enabled )` does the same from code. A window kept on top paints above every window that is not, even after another one is focused or opened. Focus itself is unchanged: the window the user last focused is still `getFocused()` and still gets the focus/blur events, it just paints under the kept-on-top band. Several windows can be kept on top at once and stack among themselves in focus order; a child window comes up with an owner that is kept on top. Fullscreen still covers everything. The flag is saved with the session, and each flip fires `os.window.always-on-top-changed`.
+
+```javascript
+wp.os.windowManager.setAlwaysOnTop( 'edit-php', true );
+wp.os.windowManager.getById( 'edit-php' ).alwaysOnTop; // true
+```
